{"t": 1794124767.2178369, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Production reconciliation regression caused by this change (commit 8c2f1d0): Sentry [LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/?query=LEDGER-WORKER-9A), first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3, reports ReconciliationMismatch: expected 1100 minor units, got 1099.\n\nThe commit diff changes `round(amount_minor * rate)` to `int(amount_minor * rate)` in worker/rates.py. `int()` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. A local reproducer, `convert(1000, 1.0999)`, returns 1099 with truncation and 1100 after restoring the previous `round(...)` implementation.\n\nFixed locally in worker/rates.py by restoring `round(amount_minor * rate)`. Added regression coverage for rounding up/down, negative amounts, ties (preserving the previous round-to-even behavior), zero, and integer return type. Validation: `python -m pytest -q` \u2014 6 passed. This is a local fix, not a deployed change.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
